{"task_id": "HumanEval/17", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef parse_music(music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Parses an ASCII music string into a list of beat durations.\n    It recognizes 'o' (4 beats), 'o|' (2 beats), and '.|' (1 beat).\n    \"\"\"\n    NOTE_PATTERNS = {\n        'o|': 2,\n        '.|': 1,\n        'o': 4,\n    }\n\n    # Sort patterns by length in descending order to ensure longer patterns are matched first,\n    # preventing cases where 'o' might be matched before 'o|'.\n    sorted_patterns = sorted(NOTE_PATTERNS.items(), key=lambda item: len(item[0]), reverse=True)\n\n    beats: List[int] = []\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(music_string):\n        # Skip any whitespace characters\n        if music_string[i].isspace():\n            i += 1\n            continue\n\n        matched = False\n        # Attempt to match current segment of the string with known note patterns\n        for pattern, beat_value in sorted_patterns:\n            if music_string.startswith(pattern, i):\n                beats.append(beat_value)\n                i += len(pattern)\n                matched = True\n                break  # Found a match, move to the next segment of the string\n\n        # If no known pattern matched a non-space character, advance pointer to avoid infinite loop\n        # and implicitly skip unrecognized characters as per simplest logic and no explicit error requirement\n        if not matched:\n            i += 1\n\n    return beats"}
