{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = l[:]  # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list\n\n    elements_to_sort = []\n    indices_to_replace = []\n    for i, item in enumerate(l):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            elements_to_sort.append(item)\n            indices_to_replace.append(i)\n\n    elements_to_sort.sort()  # Sort the extracted elements\n\n    for i, sorted_val in zip(indices_to_replace, elements_to_sort):\n        result_list[i] = sorted_val\n\n    return result_list"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    >>> sort_third([1, 2, 3])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> sort_third([5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2])\n    [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n    \"\"\"\n    indices_to_sort = []\n    values_to_sort = []\n\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            indices_to_sort.append(i)\n            values_to_sort.append(l[i])\n\n    values_to_sort.sort()\n\n    result_list = list(l)\n\n    for i, original_index in enumerate(indices_to_sort):\n        result_list[original_index] = values_to_sort[i]\n\n    return result_list"}
