{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string encoded by shifting alphabetic characters forward by 5.\n    Non-alphabetic characters remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    shift_amount = 5  # Fixed shift amount for decoding (backward)\n\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            start_ord = ord('a')\n            decoded_char_ord = (ord(char) - start_ord - shift_amount) % 26 + start_ord\n            decoded_chars.append(chr(decoded_char_ord))\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            start_ord = ord('A')\n            decoded_char_ord = (ord(char) - start_ord - shift_amount) % 26 + start_ord\n            decoded_chars.append(chr(decoded_char_ord))\n        else:\n            decoded_chars.append(char)\n\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
